      "message": "This is commented out, is that intended ? (if yes the comment should explain why).\n\nIf you\u0027re having trouble using internal tethering API, you might have to use framework-connectivity-internal-test-defaults (which is a hack that allows building against hidden API of bootclasspath classes, because normally the API stubs are earlier in the bootclasspath, so even if you add the .impl to the libs it will link against the API stub class in priority, which won\u0027t have hidden symbols).\n\nframework-connectivity-internal-test-defaults needs to be updated to use framework-tethering-pre-jarjar instead of .impl though.",
